WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.590
A “panacea” is defined as a remedy for
all difficulties and diseases.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.380
It is a medicine, potion, or other item that
can pull a patient back from the brink of

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.679
death and save someone from even the worst
of circumstances, a “cure-all.”

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:21.590
It’s a wonderful idea, one that would save
countless lives, put a stop to untold, needless

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.830
suffering, and improve the human experience
on a permanent, global scale.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.430
Unfortunately, anyone claiming to have the
solution to all problems is likely just trying

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.870
to sell you something.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.760
Unless, of course, that person works at the
SCP Foundation.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.930
Then, they just might be telling you the truth,
because they just might be telling you about

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.930
SCP-500.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:51.320
SCP-500, also known as The Panacea, is completely
unassuming in appearance.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:56.390
All it consists of is a small plastic pill
bottle, filled with exactly forty-seven red

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.660
pills.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.500
This is all that remains of the world’s
only known miracle-cure.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.300
When the pills were first discovered by the
Foundation, they were used in a variety of

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:11.320
experiments in order to determine the limits
- if any - of their curative powers.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:16.620
They tested the pills on everything from diseases
like cancer to physical injuries like a broken

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.620
femur.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:23.060
In each and every case, one pill taken orally
cured the test subject of all symptoms within

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.800
a matter of hours.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.170
After determining that SCP-500 could treat
natural ailments, the Foundation’s scientists

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.550
decided to apply it to more unnatural ills.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:40.420
Two pills were authorized for use with SCP-008,
to be administered to Class D personnel who

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.000
had been exposed to it.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.500
At the time of this experiment’s approval,
there were 57 pills in the can.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:53.200
SCP-008 is a complex prion, or a misfolded
protein with the ability to change the shape

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.410
of correctly formed variants of the same protein.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:01.310
Prions are considered to be the cause of Mad
Cow Disease, among many other debilitating

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.100
neurodegenerative diseases.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.040
SCP-008 is no exception to the devastation.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:13.090
It takes what is terrifying about other prion
diseases, the loss of cognition, the onset

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:16.990
of dementia, the certain death, and cranks
it up to 11.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:22.220
20 hours after the onset of symptoms, the
infected person will slip into a coma, but

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.730
that is not the end of their suffering.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.200
The nervous system is damaged and the cells
have begun to necrotize, but the infected

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.470
person is still able to move.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:37.690
They shamble around on two legs, they crawl,
they grab, and they bite.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:42.750
They seek out stimuli that indicate the presence
of a living, uninfected human, and they will

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.270
attempt to devour it.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:49.710
The only way to stop an infected individual
is to completely destroy their brain.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.610
Essentially, it is a zombie plague.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:58.970
Understandably, the Foundation has a vested
interest in curing and containing SCP-008,

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.750
and so the promise of the Panacea was an enticing
one.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:07.450
For the purposes of the experiment, a member
of the Class D personnel was randomly selected

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.490
and exposed to SCP-008.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:15.970
Within three hours, he began to exhibit symptoms,
running a fever of 105 degrees and coughing

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.490
and vomiting uncontrollably.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:23.750
Wanting to see if it would be possible to
use SCP-500 as a cure even in the latest stages

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:29.030
of the disease, the scientists conducting
the experiment allowed the symptoms to progress,

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.050
with the test subject eventually slipping
into a coma.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:37.050
Once comatose, the cell degeneration quickened,
until he began to move again.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:42.349
His dull, unfocused eyes roamed around the
room, and he lurched toward a member of the

00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:45.129
research staff, biting down on her arm.

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:49.160
Of course, she was clad in Hazmat gear in
order to prevent infection, but the Class

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.239
D no longer had the cognitive capacity to
understand that.

00:03:53.239 --> 00:03:58.440
The researcher seized the opportunity to wrench
his jaws open and stuff one of the SCP-500

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.000
pills down his throat.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.030
Once the pill had been swallowed, she vacated
the room and the test subject was quarantined.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:09.879
After two hours, the research team returned
to investigate the results of their test.

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:13.050
What they found was something amazing.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:18.329
Sitting in the cell was a completely lucid,
healthy, if a bit confused, man with no signs

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:21.729
of the disease that had previously ravaged
his body.

00:04:21.729 --> 00:04:27.449
The Panacea was able to cure SCP-008, even
at its most advanced stages.

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:34.379
So, they knew that SCP-500 could cure a prion
disease like 008, but what else could it cure?

00:04:34.379 --> 00:04:37.960
What was the extent of its marvelous medical
power if any?

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.199
Could it cure an ailment with virtually no
basis in modern medical understanding?

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:46.250
Next, one pill was approved and allocated
for testing with SCP-409.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:52.900
SCP-409 is a rock formation resembling a large
quartz crystal.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:57.559
It is kept in a sealed granite case, and no
one is permitted to touch it with any substance

00:04:57.559 --> 00:05:01.990
other than granite, unless during active experimentation.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:07.659
Anyone who comes into physical contact with
SCP-409 suffers a peculiar, and nightmarish,

00:05:07.659 --> 00:05:14.830
fate: they will immediately begin to crystallize,
their body effectively turning into rock.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:19.479
The crystallization occurs at a rate of roughly
one inch per minute, and will continue until

00:05:19.479 --> 00:05:23.029
the victim’s entire body, inside and out,
has solidified.

00:05:23.029 --> 00:05:29.210
It is an incredibly painful process, and thought
to be completely irreversible.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:34.949
Subject 409-D5 was chosen at random from a
group of Class D personnel as the guinea pig

00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:37.909
for the next SCP-500 experiment.

00:05:37.909 --> 00:05:42.810
He was exposed to SCP-409, touching it with
his index finger.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:46.770
This small touch was more than enough to seal
his fate.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:51.919
Upon contact, the finger immediately began
to crystallize, spreading up his hand, his

00:05:51.919 --> 00:05:56.469
wrist, and his arm over the course of several
minutes as he screamed in agony.

00:05:56.469 --> 00:06:01.360
It was difficult to administer SCP-500 with
all of the screaming, but a researcher was

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.949
able to close his mouth long enough for the
pill to be swallowed.

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:10.370
Within a few hours, the Foundation researchers
watched as the crystallization process slowed,

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.830
and then stopped.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:16.699
After nine days in a Foundation hospital ward,
the crystallization process had completely

00:06:16.699 --> 00:06:19.839
reversed, and the man was returned to normal.

00:06:19.839 --> 00:06:24.729
He still reported phantom pain in the formerly
crystallized parts of his body, but even that

00:06:24.729 --> 00:06:27.399
cleared up after several more days.

00:06:27.399 --> 00:06:33.840
After the incredible success of the SCP-008
and SCP-409 trials, the Foundation was desperate

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.279
to synthesize their own version of SCP-500.

00:06:37.279 --> 00:06:41.889
A multitude of experiments were performed
in an attempt to isolate the active ingredient

00:06:41.889 --> 00:06:46.969
in the pills, but every time they found what
appeared to be the miracle aspect of the anomalous

00:06:46.969 --> 00:06:51.550
pills, they found that they were unable to
synthesize it and have it produce the same

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.659
results as the real thing.

00:06:53.659 --> 00:06:58.210
Extensive drug trials were conducted, leaving
a trail of injured and dead D Class Personnel

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.479
in their wake.

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:03.770
With the traditional pharmacological route
eliminated, the Foundation decided to expose

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:09.379
some of the pills to a variety of other SCPs
in an attempt to somehow recreate or amplify

00:07:09.379 --> 00:07:10.860
their effects.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:16.129
Most of the results were lackluster or completely
uneventful, however, some did yield notable

00:07:16.129 --> 00:07:17.149
results.

00:07:17.149 --> 00:07:23.539
One pill was taken from SCP-500 and placed
inside of SCP-914, which is a large clockwork

00:07:23.539 --> 00:07:28.639
device with a multitude of settings - ranging
from Very Fine to Rough - that is capable

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:31.349
of transforming matter in various ways.

00:07:31.349 --> 00:07:36.270
The pill was run through SCP-914 on the “Fine”
setting and the machine produced a small,

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:41.689
silver locket, which would later be classified
as SCP-427.

00:07:41.689 --> 00:07:46.459
SCP-427 retained some of the healing properties
of its original form, able to regenerate damaged

00:07:46.459 --> 00:07:51.919
cells and purge infection from the body when
it is opened and exposed to a living subject.

00:07:51.919 --> 00:07:55.300
During testing, it was able to cure the common
cold in a matter of minutes.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:01.089
However, unlike SCP-500, the locket produced
notable negative side effects.

00:08:01.089 --> 00:08:05.870
Prolonged exposure to SCP-427’s healing
properties increased cell regeneration and

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:10.050
the optimization of bodily systems beyond
a healthy threshold.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:14.569
Exposure for more than an hour turned the
test subjects into shapeless masses of tissue,

00:08:14.569 --> 00:08:16.789
nicknamed “flesh beasts”.

00:08:16.789 --> 00:08:20.839
These flesh beasts are highly aggressive and
will attack anything in sight unless they

00:08:20.839 --> 00:08:22.479
are put down.

00:08:22.479 --> 00:08:28.650
SCP-427 was intended to be a potential replacement
for SCP-500 once the limited number of pills

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:34.330
ran out, but the potential risks of its use
have led to it being shelved indefinitely.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:39.140
With all attempts to create a different, yet
equally effective version of SCP-500 ending

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:43.810
in failure, the Foundation instead tried to
find a way to duplicate it.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:48.460
In one case, an experiment was conducted with
the intent to produce more of the Panacea

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:54.200
pills, not using chemistry and compounding,
but instead opting for a much more unusual

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.200
method.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.120
After a request was submitted and approved,
five pills from the bottle were selected to

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.020
be exposed to SCP-038.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:07.620
SCP-038 is a highly unique plant, resembling
a common apple tree.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.770
However, it can grow far more than just apples.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:15.510
The tree can clone any object that touches
its bark, producing the clone on its branches

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.140
where an ordinary tree would bear fruit.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:22.580
The five allocated pills were touched to the
fabric of the tree, and sure enough, clones

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.650
of the red capsules began to sprout within
seconds.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:31.510
But while the tree was able to clone pills
that looked identical to SCP-500, their effectiveness

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.160
was sorely lacking compared to the originals.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:39.880
Cloned pills were only approximately 30% effective
in curing the infections they were used to

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:44.090
treat, as opposed to the 100% effectiveness
with the real deal.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:48.390
The cloned pills were set aside for treatment
of less severe infections, and all of the

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.080
originals were returned to their storage container.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.400
Well, almost all of them.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:57.660
As the experiment was wrapping up, a D-class
participating in the experiment managed to

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.750
pocket one of the five pills allocated for
the test.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.890
The pill’s absence was not noticed until
the following day, at which point it had already

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.590
been ingested by the thief.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:11.470
When interrogated, the man admitted that he
had stolen the pill in order to cure a particularly

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:16.460
nasty hangover, after his usual method of
pickle juice, a bacon sandwich, and aspirin

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.690
had failed.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:24.120
The employee was promptly terminated, and
security around SCP-500 was tightened significantly.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:28.810
Following this incident, no personnel below
Level Three were permitted to handle SCP-500

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.380
in any capacity.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:37.150
When it was initially brought into the Foundation,
there were approximately 57 pills in SCP-500’s

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:40.480
container and currently, only 47 remain.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:45.690
Due to the limited amount of pills, and inability
thus far to duplicate them in an equivalently

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:51.980
effective form, experimentation with SCP-500
has been drastically limited.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:56.300
Most requests for experimentation or allocation
of pills are promptly denied.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:00.470
These requests have included a Dr. Gibbons
who asked that two pills be given to him for

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:06.960
his personal medkit, as well as a proposed
experiment involving SCP-253, a group of cells

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.430
which bear some strong resemblances to cancer.

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:14.770
Several concerned personnel at the Foundation
have worried that SCP-500 may have another

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:20.220
anomalous effect, that it may cause obsessive
fixation in those who spend a great deal of

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:26.020
time with it, leading them to experiment with
it again and again, unable to let it go until

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.720
they crack an unsolvable code.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:34.550
This has been immediately dismissed as trivial
and unfounded by the SCP-500 research team,

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:39.200
surely their obsessive work with the pills
is their own choice, but perhaps the concerned

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.900
parties have a point.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:45.030
After all, there are few things more compelling
than a miracle cure and there is arguably

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:50.280
no greater scientific discovery that could
be made, no higher mountain that one could

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:51.280
climb.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:56.630
And there is nothing more maddening than having
that life saving pill in your grasp and watch

00:11:56.630 --> 00:12:03.010
the number dwindle down one pill at a time,
like grains of sand slipping between your

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:04.050
fingers.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:10.260
With only 47 pills left and no way to recreate
them on the horizon, perhaps the Panacea is

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:15.820
both a blessing and a curse, a tantalizing
glimpse at what humanity could have but will

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:17.980
never truly achieve.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:22.220
But hey, maybe they’ll crack the code if
they just try one more experiment, and why

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.220
not try?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:30.050
There’ll still be 46 left… and then 45…
and then… well let’s just hope they figure

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:33.650
it out before they truly are all gone.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:39.990
Now go check out “SCP-999 - The Tickle Monster”
and “The Eye Pods - SCP-131” for more

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:40.870
helpful anomalies!

